1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,607
A merchant may run several websites, so which one is allowed to take payments?

2
00:00:04,607 --> 00:00:11,547
A sales point is one website, with its own settings, card schemes, and allowed return addresses.

3
00:00:11,547 --> 00:00:18,404
The deal also fixes how many days refunds are allowed, and a longer window needs a written reason, such as a warranty.

4
00:00:18,404 --> 00:00:21,333
It starts as a draft, and cannot take payments yet.

5
00:00:21,333 --> 00:00:26,071
Two admins check the site: a real shop, real goods, and a legal business.

6
00:00:26,071 --> 00:00:30,166
A failed check records its findings, and the sales point stays closed.

7
00:00:30,166 --> 00:00:33,047
A passed check lets the sales point go active.

8
00:00:33,047 --> 00:00:37,607
While it is active, the merchant cannot quietly change the website address.

9
00:00:37,607 --> 00:00:43,952
The payment module will ask one internal question on every request: is this sales point active?

10
00:00:43,952 --> 00:00:49,059
Next, a second module appears, and with it, copied code we must remove.

